articleSummary:
- Senate committee votes to refer Anthony Fauci for contempt of Congress over alleged noncompliance, with Rand Paul to forward the matter to the DOJ, framed as criminalizing scientific guidance rather than pursuing COVID-19 origins. Cyclosporiasis outbreaks span 47 states, totaling 10,468 lab-confirmed cases from May 1 to Aug 3, plus 12,255 cases awaiting confirmation, and two deaths in Michigan as of Aug 4. Measles cases in the United States have reached their highest level since 1991, challenging the eradication status declared in 2000. An Mpox-related incident involved inactivated samples transported from the Republic of Congo to Detroit, prompting investigations. The article places these outbreaks in the context of a broader political campaign against infection-disease researchers, amid 
- Erica Schwartz was confirmed CDC director on 2026-08-07, taking the helm during three concurrent outbreaks. Measles now has 2,371 confirmed cases as of July 30, 2026—the year’s highest tally since 1991 and above 2025’s total (2,289); 37 new outbreaks this year and 94% of cases outbreak-associated, with PAHO to review U.S. measles elimination status in November. Cyclosporiasis tied to recalled Taylor Farms de Mexico iceberg lettuce marks the largest U.S. outbreak on record, with more than 10,000 lab-confirmed domestically acquired cases since May 1, and Michigan alone reporting 12,485 cases and two deaths. A jalapeño outbreak linked to Sinaloa, Mexico, distributed by Coast Citrus Distributors accounts for 345 illnesses across 27 states, 36 hospitalizations, no deaths; onset June 19–July 20;
- Erica Schwartz was confirmed by the Senate (51-44) as CDC director, becoming the agency’s first African American female leader. As of August 5, 2026, the United States faces two major foodborne outbreaks: cyclosporiasis and Salmonella. Cyclosporiasis has spread to 15 states, with 6,358 cases, 278 hospitalizations, and 2 deaths; investigations point to Taylor Farms lettuce, and six additional states (Arkansas, Iowa, Missouri, Nebraska, New Hampshire, North Carolina) are affected, suggesting a common Cyclospora source linked to a Taylor Farms facility in central Mexico that has a history of prior outbreaks. Salmonella infections total 345 cases and 36 hospitalizations across 27 states, tied to Mexican peppers distributed by Coast Citrus Distributors from Sinaloa; Chipotle and QDOBA have halt
